  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TUI Academy Dominican Republic 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMMARY. In the Dominican Republic, youth, and young women in particular, are denied the chance to go to school and gain access to a decent job. Tourism and Hospitality (T&amp;H) is an important sector with many job opportunities. The TUI Academy is created by TUI Care Foundation and Plan International to ensure 150 youths (aged 18-29, at least 60% female) at risk of Commercial Sexual Exploitation (CSE) in La Altagracia, Dominican Republic, are socially and economically empowered by June 2025. The TUI Academy offers them vocational skills training based on the demands from the T&amp;H market, life skills training which includes communicating in English, and an internship at a resort or hotel that is owned/contracted by TUI. The project aims to ensure these youths can protect themselves from CSE and increases their opportunities for obtaining decent work in the T&amp;H sector.</narrative>
  </description>
